===Etymology===
{{etymon|en|:inh|enm:circle<ety:bor<fro:cercle>>|tree=1}}
{{root|en|ine-pro|*(s)ker- (turn)}}
From {{inh|en|enm|circle}}, {{m|enm|cercle}}, from {{der|en|fro|cercle}} and {{der|en|la|circulus}}, diminutive of {{der|en|la|circus|t=circle, circus}}, from {{der|en|grc|κίρκος|t=circle, ring}}, related to {{cog|ang|hring|t=ring}}. Compare also {{cog|ang|ċircul|t=circle, zodiac}}, which came from the same Latin source. {{surf|en|la:circus|alt1=circ(us)|-ule|alt2=-(u)le}}.

